N=[]
def n(*t):N.append(t)
U='upper-limb'
n('radial-collateral-ligament-of-elbow','Radial collateral ligament of the elbow','Ligamentum collaterale radiale',[],U,'On the lateral side of the elbow, from the lateral epicondyle of the humerus to the annular ligament of the radius.','A fan-shaped band on the lateral side of the elbow capsule that blends with the annular ligament and the origin of the supinator.','Resists varus (inward-directed) stress and helps keep the radial head against the humerus.','Injury, often with elbow dislocation or after surgery on the lateral epicondyle, can cause posterolateral rotatory instability of the elbow.')
n('ulnar-collateral-ligament-of-elbow','Ulnar collateral ligament of the elbow','Ligamentum collaterale ulnare',['medial collateral ligament of the elbow'],U,'On the medial side of the elbow, from the medial epicondyle of the humerus to the coronoid process and olecranon of the ulna.','A triangular ligament with anterior, posterior and transverse bands on the medial side of the elbow capsule.','The anterior band is the main restraint to valgus (outward-directed) stress at the elbow.','Repeated throwing can strain or tear the anterior band; reconstruction is often called Tommy John surgery.')
n('radial-collateral-ligament-of-wrist','Radial collateral ligament of the wrist','Ligamentum collaterale carpi radiale',[],U,'On the thumb side of the wrist, from the styloid process of the radius to the scaphoid and trapezium.','A short band on the radial side of the radiocarpal joint capsule.','Limits excessive ulnar deviation and stabilises the radial side of the wrist.','Can be sprained in falls on the outstretched hand, often alongside scaphoid injury.')
n('ulnar-collateral-ligament-of-wrist','Ulnar collateral ligament of the wrist','Ligamentum collaterale carpi ulnare',[],U,'On the little-finger side of the wrist, from the styloid process of the ulna to the triquetrum and pisiform.','A band on the ulnar side of the radiocarpal joint capsule.','Limits excessive radial deviation and stabilises the ulnar side of the wrist.','Often injured together with the triangular fibrocartilage complex in ulnar-sided wrist pain.')
n('radioscaphocapitate-ligament','Radioscaphocapitate ligament','Ligamentum radioscaphocapitatum',[],U,'On the palm side of the wrist, from the radial styloid process across the waist of the scaphoid to the capitate.','A strong extrinsic palmar wrist ligament that supports the scaphoid.','Acts as a sling around the scaphoid and limits its rotation when the wrist moves.','Disruption contributes to carpal instability and is assessed in wrist injuries.')
n('ulnolunate-ligament','Ulnolunate ligament','Ligamentum ulnolunatum',[],U,'On the palm side of the wrist, from the triangular fibrocartilage complex at the ulna to the lunate.','A palmar ulnocarpal ligament, one of the supports of the ulnar side of the wrist.','Links the ulnar side of the forearm to the proximal carpal row.','Involved in injuries of the triangular fibrocartilage complex.')
n('ulnotriquetral-ligament','Ulnotriquetral ligament','Ligamentum ulnotriquetrum',[],U,'On the palm side of the wrist, from the triangular fibrocartilage complex at the ulna to the triquetrum.','A palmar ulnocarpal ligament running with the ulnolunate ligament.','Stabilises the ulnar side of the carpus against the forearm.','Injured together with the triangular fibrocartilage complex in ulnar-sided wrist pain.')
n('deep-transverse-metacarpal-ligament','Deep transverse metacarpal ligament','Ligamentum metacarpale transversum profundum',[],U,'In the palm at the heads of the second to fifth metacarpals.','Short ligaments that join the palmar ligaments of neighbouring metacarpophalangeal joints.','Holds the metacarpal heads together and limits spreading of the fingers.','Rarely injured in isolation; it forms part of the structure around the finger knuckle joints.')
n('scaphotrapeziotrapezoidal-ligament','Scaphotrapeziotrapezoidal ligament','Ligamentum scaphotrapeziotrapezoideum',[],U,'In the wrist, joining the scaphoid to the trapezium and trapezoid.','A ligament complex on the radial side of the distal carpal row.','Stabilises the scaphoid against the distal carpal row.','Injury can lead to scaphoid rotation and radial-sided wrist pain.')
